    "created_at": "2020-11-10T08:11:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-10T08:11:59Z",
    "body": "Well, I would see value in making it ltr by default in _most_ languages. Of course, developers can set the correct direction manually, but I use Hebrew RTL websites all the time, and I see that many developers don't do it, and making a better default would be nice. (I'd also love to see the same for credit card numbers.)\r\n\r\nHowever, it shouldn't _always_ be ltr. Languages written in the [N'Ko alphabet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N'Ko_script) would have to be rtl, because they write numbers from right to left.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
